WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:04.000
-Welcome, everybody. Welcome, welcome, welcome, welcome

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.434
to "The Tonight Show." You're here. You made it.

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:09.901
♪♪

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:12.601
Let's get to some news. Well, guys, President Biden says

00:00:12.601 --> 00:00:15.601
that he plans to run for re-election in 2024.

00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:17.000
Meanwhile, at a rally this weekend,

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.267
President Trump also hinted at running.

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:22.100
It's big news, but all I can think about is Taylor Swift

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.934
being on the show tonight, so...

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:25.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.834
So you know what that means.

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:34.133
It's time for "The News (Taylor's Version)."

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.834
Here we go. [ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:38.334
♪♪

00:00:38.334 --> 00:00:41.501
So, Biden and Trump are both running for re-election,

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:43.400
and they've got major "bad blood,"

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.234
which everyone knows "all too well."

00:00:46.234 --> 00:00:48.968
Of course, Trump has quite the "reputation."

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:51.701
Every other day, he's like, "I did something bad,"

00:00:51.701 --> 00:00:53.167
and Biden has to be like,

00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:54.801
"This is why we can't have nice things,"

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:58.033
which is why this could be the most dramatic election

00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:01.234
ever -- more -- Importantly --

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:04.234
"Evermore" importantly, they both need running mates.

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:07.000
Biden is looking at Kamala like, "You belong with me,"

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.200
while Trump is looking at Mike Pence like,

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.534
"We are never ever getting back together."

00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:15.934
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:17.534
Like, ever.

00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:19.601
Pence is actually considering a run of his own,

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:21.667
but everyone is like, "I forgot that you existed."

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:22.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:25.467
"Long story short," everyone is tired of politics.

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:27.634
But, hey, "you need to calm down,"

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:29.901
"shake it off," and get "ready for it,"

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:32.300
because "'tis the damn season." So --

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:37.701
Go get your voting "card again,"

00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:39.100
head to the polls --

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.801
Yeah, that was a stretch, that one.

00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:43.267
Head to the polls and fill in every "blank space."

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:45.601
It doesn't matter if you're blue or "red"

00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:47.300
or even a "lavender haze."

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:50.100
You've got to let your voice be heard,

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.567
both in 2024 and during the midterms in "'22."

00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:55.934
This has been "The News (Taylor's Version)."

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:57.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:57.801 --> 00:02:00.434
♪♪

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:02.167
"Card again." -Yeah.

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:04.167
-No, that was awful. That was a stretch there.

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:06.934
Yeah, that's right. Biden intends to run again.

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:09.534
And in a recent interview on MSNBC, he was asked

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:11.267
about his concerns over his age.

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:13.167
Check out the President's response right here.

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:16.100
-I think it's a legitimate thing to be concerned

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.367
about anyone's age, including mine.

00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:20.334
That's not how I feel.

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:23.234
I can't even say the age I'm gonna be.

00:02:23.234 --> 00:02:25.934
I can't even get it out of my mouth.

00:02:25.934 --> 00:02:29.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.601 --> 00:02:31.100
-I've heard of people dancing around their age,

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.300
but I've never seen someone

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.200
actually dance around their age, like...

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:38.734
Eventually, a middle-school nun stepped in like,

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:39.901
"Leave room for the Holy Ghost.

00:02:39.901 --> 00:02:41.968
Leave -- Leave room for the Holy Ghost."

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:43.567
Secret Service didn't know what to do.

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:45.667
They were like, "Should we step in or give them alone time?

00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:47.868
What's the call here?" [ Laughter ]

00:02:47.868 --> 00:02:49.734
Some more political news -- over the weekend,

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:51.834
former president Trump held a rally in Texas,

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:53.634
and I noticed that he had some trouble

00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:55.400
with the word "smuggler." Watch this.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.601
-They've deliberately surrendered our border

00:02:57.601 --> 00:03:00.200
to vicious coyotes and drug smaller --

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.901
I mean, these drug smug--

00:03:01.901 --> 00:03:04.501
The smuggler. A smuggler!

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:07.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:09.334
-"These drug snugglers -- drug smuckers --

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:12.534
drug snickerdoodles, they --" [ Laughter ]

00:03:12.534 --> 00:03:14.334
He sounds like he took whatever illegal drug

00:03:14.334 --> 00:03:17.501
is being "smullered" across the border.

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:19.667
Sounds like a guy trying to do his first Wordle.

00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:23.701
It's like, "Small? Smug? Is smulg a word?

00:03:23.701 --> 00:03:25.367
I'm gonna try 'smulg' anyway. Why not?

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:27.300
Let's see. Oh, I'm very smart."

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.133
Speaking of Trump, the January 6th Committee

00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:31.968
announced that they have subpoenaed the former president.

00:03:31.968 --> 00:03:33.634
Yep, Trump's already bragging like,

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:34.834
"I've got the biggest subpoena.

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:36.934
I've been saying it for years.

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:39.033
Nobody's subpoena is bigger than mine."

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:42.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:43.400
Yep, the committee was like,

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.534
"Here's a federal document that you can keep."

00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:47.367
Yeah. [ Audience groans ]

00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:50.434
Some big news from overseas -- today, Britain announced that

00:03:50.434 --> 00:03:53.434
Rishi Sunak is going to be their new prime minister

00:03:53.434 --> 00:03:56.901
after Liz Truss lasted only six weeks in office.

00:03:56.901 --> 00:03:59.033
Yeah, when he showed up to his new office, people were like,

00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:00.734
"You can unpack your things, but I wouldn't hang up

00:04:00.734 --> 00:04:02.901
anything on the walls." [ Laughter ]

00:04:02.901 --> 00:04:05.133
Yeah, on Thursday, after 45 days in office,

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:07.067
Liz Truss announced her resignation

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:09.100
as prime minister of Britain.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.267
Let's take a look back

00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:12.334
on all the greatest moments of Liz Truss.

00:04:12.334 --> 00:04:15.767
♪♪

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:16.834
-Good afternoon.

00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:18.434
♪♪

00:04:18.434 --> 00:04:20.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:28.000
-Well, some sports news -- the World Series matchup

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.501
is set with the Houston Astros

00:04:29.501 --> 00:04:31.400
taking on the Philadelphia Phillies.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:32.934
[ Cheers and applause ] And, of course --

00:04:32.934 --> 00:04:35.400
♪♪

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.467
Of course, the fans from Philadelphia are super pumped.

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:39.767
Check out this video.

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:42.467
-Let's go, Philly! [ Laughter ]

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:44.033
-I'm feeling great!

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:45.834
Four more dub!

00:04:45.834 --> 00:04:47.100
-Come on, Phillies!

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:50.100
Four more! World Series, baby!

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.701
-We got married on Friday, and the Phillies won!

00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:55.133
-This is the best part of the weekend by far!

00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:57.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:57.801 --> 00:05:01.534
-Oh! "By far"?

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:03.367
-"By far." -Oh, my God.

00:05:03.367 --> 00:05:05.567
-A lot of people have videos of the moment they got married,

00:05:05.567 --> 00:05:07.067
but very few have a video of the moment

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:08.734
their marriage fell apart. You know what I'm saying?

00:05:08.734 --> 00:05:10.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.501 --> 00:05:12.834
Finally, scientists in Japan have gotten closer to finding

00:05:12.834 --> 00:05:14.868
a cure for baldness after they were able

00:05:14.868 --> 00:05:17.367
to grow hair follicles in a lab.

00:05:17.367 --> 00:05:19.367
Well, they actually grew them just outside the lab,

00:05:19.367 --> 00:05:22.400
then they combed them over into the lab.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:23.968
Some fun holiday news --

00:05:23.968 --> 00:05:26.234
Mariah Carey just announced that, this December,

00:05:26.234 --> 00:05:28.834
she's playing a Christmas show at Madison Square Garden.

00:05:28.834 --> 00:05:31.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:31.834 --> 00:05:34.334
Mariah Carey Christmas show in New York City.

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:35.834
When they heard that, The Rockettes were like,

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:38.234
"Stay in your lane, girl!"

00:05:38.234 --> 00:05:39.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:39.334 --> 00:05:40.901
"Stay in your lane!"

00:05:40.901 --> 00:05:43.267
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.267 --> 00:05:44.834
-Wow.

00:05:44.834 --> 00:05:46.934
-So, if you want to hear "All I Want for Christmas is You,"

00:05:46.934 --> 00:05:48.300
you can either go to the concert

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:50.567
or any CVS from now until January.

00:05:50.567 --> 00:05:51.968
There you go. [ Laughter ]

00:05:51.968 --> 00:05:55.267
Some other New York news -- yesterday, Senator Ted Cruz

00:05:55.267 --> 00:05:58.367
was on "The View," and he got heckled and cursed at

00:05:58.367 --> 00:06:00.067
by some people in the audience.

00:06:00.067 --> 00:06:01.601
[ Cheers ]

00:06:01.601 --> 00:06:03.000
Don't worry -- after a few minutes,

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:05.767
security was able to remove Joy and Whoopi from the set,

00:06:05.767 --> 00:06:09.267
and so then... [ Laughter ]

00:06:09.267 --> 00:06:11.400
Some of the hecklers were climate activists.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.701
The rest were a group of moms who were mad that Ted Cruz

00:06:13.701 --> 00:06:15.300
was the guest they were seeing on "The View."

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:17.133
It's like, "Come on!" [ Laughter ]

00:06:17.133 --> 00:06:19.501
Some news from Washington -- today, President Biden

00:06:19.501 --> 00:06:21.634
got the updated COVID booster shot

00:06:21.634 --> 00:06:24.100
and encouraged Americans to do the same.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:27.334
That's right -- a 79-year-old getting a shot on TV.

00:06:27.334 --> 00:06:29.534
You know how excited everyone was for Taylor Swift's

00:06:29.534 --> 00:06:31.567
album to drop? This wasn't like that.

00:06:31.567 --> 00:06:33.968
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.968 --> 00:06:37.567
Yep, this was Biden's fifth COVID shot.

00:06:37.567 --> 00:06:39.033
Most Americans are like, "I'm just gonna wait

00:06:39.033 --> 00:06:40.634
till they all come out and binge 'em all at once."

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:42.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.467 --> 00:06:44.501
Well, I saw this today -- Bob Woodward released

00:06:44.501 --> 00:06:46.400
an audiobook of his 20 interviews

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.400
with former president Trump, called "The Trump Tapes."

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:51.267
And I didn't know this, but apparently, at one point,

00:06:51.267 --> 00:06:53.501
Woodward asked Trump some rapid-fire questions.

00:06:53.501 --> 00:06:54.667
Have you heard of this? -Really?

00:06:54.667 --> 00:06:56.367
-Yeah, it's fascinating. Take a listen to this.

00:07:21.801 --> 00:07:25.901
-Yeah, just very interesting. Rapid-fire questions.

00:07:25.901 --> 00:07:27.634
-Wow. -Pillsbury Doughboy.

00:07:27.634 --> 00:07:30.300
-Wow! -Guys, this is very exciting.

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:32.267
We're only six days away from Halloween.

00:07:32.267 --> 00:07:36.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:36.634 --> 00:07:39.000
And I heard that some of this year's most popular costumes

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:41.834
are Spider-Man, the "Stranger Things" kids,

00:07:41.834 --> 00:07:46.801
and dinosaurs, while the least popular is Anti-Semitic Guy.

00:07:46.801 --> 00:07:51.634
And, uh... [ Audience groans, laughs ]

00:07:51.634 --> 00:07:53.133
-Come on!

00:07:53.133 --> 00:07:54.801
[ Cheers and applause ] -Least popular.

00:07:54.801 --> 00:07:57.934
The least popular costume. -Yeah.

00:07:57.934 --> 00:08:00.434
-Yeah. Everyone is talking about this --

00:08:00.434 --> 00:08:03.400
today, after weeks of public pressure, Adidas finally ended

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:05.300
their partnership with Kanye West

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:07.534
due to his anti-Semitic remarks.

00:08:07.534 --> 00:08:09.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:09.367 --> 00:08:10.968
I think we finally answered the question,

00:08:10.968 --> 00:08:12.934
"Is there such a thing as bad publicity?"

00:08:12.934 --> 00:08:15.701
Yes, I think there is. Yep, Kanye has now lost

00:08:15.701 --> 00:08:19.334
his deals with Adidas, Balenciaga, and Manischewitz.

00:08:19.334 --> 00:08:22.133
[ Laughter ]

00:08:22.133 --> 00:08:25.033
-Hey! -And now Gap also announced

00:08:25.033 --> 00:08:27.267
that they're pulling all Yeezy products from their stores.

00:08:27.267 --> 00:08:28.701
[ Audience oohs ] Yep.

00:08:28.701 --> 00:08:31.267
Meanwhile, TJ Maxx is like, "We'll sell whatever ya got."

00:08:31.267 --> 00:08:32.534
[ Laughter ]

00:08:32.534 --> 00:08:34.400
"We let it rip in this place."

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:36.434
[ Laughter ]

00:08:36.434 --> 00:08:38.501
Some more business news -- the Federal Trade Commission

00:08:38.501 --> 00:08:42.334
wants to hold the CEO of alcohol delivery service Drizly

00:08:42.334 --> 00:08:45.734
accountable for a 2020 data breach.

00:08:45.734 --> 00:08:47.934
In response, Drizly released this statement.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:58.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:58.467 --> 00:09:01.200
Okay. Alright.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:04.234
Well, get this -- I read that Apple is now selling a door lock

00:09:04.234 --> 00:09:07.767
for your house that you can unlock with an iPhone.

00:09:07.767 --> 00:09:09.267
Yep, so in case you lose your iPhone,

00:09:09.267 --> 00:09:11.100
make sure to keep a spare one under the mat.

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:12.734
[ Laughter ]

00:09:12.734 --> 00:09:14.834
Breaking into someone's home is about to be super easy.

00:09:14.834 --> 00:09:17.734
Just stand on the porch and yell, "Siri, unlock house!"

00:09:17.734 --> 00:09:18.968
[ Laughter ]

00:09:18.968 --> 00:09:21.267
Well, a new report says that, since the pandemic,

00:09:21.267 --> 00:09:24.968
people have gotten worse at interacting with each other.

00:09:24.968 --> 00:09:27.734
I don't think that's true. Do you agree with that, Tariq?

00:09:27.734 --> 00:09:29.167
-Good.

00:09:29.167 --> 00:09:31.200
[ Laughter ]

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:33.767
-Off to a bad start. Higgins, how you been?

00:09:33.767 --> 00:09:35.567
-Thanks. You too. [ Laughter ]

00:09:35.567 --> 00:09:37.534
-All right, 0 for 2. One last try.

00:09:37.534 --> 00:09:40.434
Let's go with Mike, the camera guy. How are you doing?

00:09:40.434 --> 00:09:42.100
-I'm well, Jimmy. Thanks for asking.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:43.434
[ Cheers and applause ] -There you go.

00:09:43.434 --> 00:09:46.434
Finally, a normal response.

00:09:46.434 --> 00:09:48.434
Well, this is wild. Due to a broken elevator,

00:09:48.434 --> 00:09:51.133
five tourists were stuck in a Grand Canyon hotel

00:09:51.133 --> 00:09:54.934
for over a day, 200 feet underground.

00:09:54.934 --> 00:09:59.100
Yep, the only person in a deeper hole is Kanye West.

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:01.667
Today, President Biden held a meeting at the White House

00:10:01.667 --> 00:10:04.667
with Israeli President Isaac Herzog.

00:10:04.667 --> 00:10:06.734
Biden and Israel's president spent hours together.

00:10:06.734 --> 00:10:08.767
They discussed Iran, Russia,

00:10:08.767 --> 00:10:11.567
and all of their favorite tracks off the new Taylor Swift album.

00:10:11.567 --> 00:10:12.934
[ Laughter ]

00:10:12.934 --> 00:10:14.601
"Lavender Haze."

00:10:14.601 --> 00:10:16.868
Meanwhile, earlier today, President Biden also announced

00:10:16.868 --> 00:10:20.000
a plan to cut hidden bank and credit-card fees

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:23.167
in an effort to give families more breathing room.

00:10:23.167 --> 00:10:24.434
Yeah.

00:10:24.434 --> 00:10:26.334
[ Cheers and applause ] Good.

00:10:26.334 --> 00:10:27.868
More breathing room. Interesting. Yeah.

00:10:27.868 --> 00:10:29.200
"Breathing room" sounds like

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:32.601
Biden's launching his own line of Skims.

00:10:32.601 --> 00:10:34.167
To be honest, I don't know if Biden

00:10:34.167 --> 00:10:36.667
is the best person to talk about giving people breathing room.

00:10:36.667 --> 00:10:38.567
But I don't know. Maybe I'm wrong. I don't know.

00:10:38.567 --> 00:10:40.968
[ Laughter ]

00:10:44.067 --> 00:10:45.767
Biden also said that he's looking to get rid of

00:10:45.767 --> 00:10:48.367
added fees on cable bills.

00:10:48.367 --> 00:10:50.000
That's great news.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:53.167
[ Cheers and applause ] That's great news.

00:10:53.167 --> 00:10:55.133
Great news for the three people who still have cable.

00:10:55.133 --> 00:10:56.667
It's amazing news.

00:10:56.667 --> 00:10:59.801
Some more news -- Russia just notified the U.S.

00:10:59.801 --> 00:11:02.834
that they would be launching nuclear-capable missiles

00:11:02.834 --> 00:11:04.767
as part of their annual nuclear exercise.

00:11:04.767 --> 00:11:05.968
Russia is just like us --

00:11:05.968 --> 00:11:07.968
they also exercise only once a year.

00:11:07.968 --> 00:11:09.234
It's great.

00:11:09.234 --> 00:11:11.267
But the U.S. is keeping a close eye on Russia.

00:11:11.267 --> 00:11:13.000
Yesterday, Biden said that it would be

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:14.801
a "serious, serious mistake"

00:11:14.801 --> 00:11:17.067
for Russia to use nuclear weapons.

00:11:17.067 --> 00:11:20.000
Wow. I haven't heard words that powerful

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.534
since FDR called Japan's attack on Pearl Harbor

00:11:22.534 --> 00:11:24.968
a "major no-no." [ Laughter ]

00:11:24.968 --> 00:11:28.167
That's right. Biden said that if Russia uses nuclear weapons

00:11:28.167 --> 00:11:31.601
they would be making a "serious, serious mistake."

00:11:31.601 --> 00:11:33.100
Yep. And he didn't stop there.

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:36.701
Next he said, "For realsies, you better not."

00:11:36.701 --> 00:11:38.200
-Wow.

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:39.901
