00:20:46.868 --> 00:20:49.267
People are like, "Okay. But what about the other countries?"

00:20:49.267 --> 00:20:51.868
[ Laughter ]

00:20:51.868 --> 00:20:53.467
Guys, of course, it's election season,

00:20:53.467 --> 00:20:55.234
and there's a weird story from Pennsylvania.

00:20:55.234 --> 00:20:57.367
Apparently, a Democrat named Mike Doyle

00:20:57.367 --> 00:21:00.334
is retiring from Congress, and the Republican candidate

00:21:00.334 --> 00:21:03.801
to replace him is actually named Mike Doyle.

00:21:03.801 --> 00:21:05.234
[ Laughter ]

00:21:05.234 --> 00:21:07.501
While the outgoing Democrat, Mike Doyle,

00:21:07.501 --> 00:21:10.734
doesn't want the Republican Mike Doyle to win his seat,

00:21:10.734 --> 00:21:12.400
so he just released this ad. Take a look.

00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:18.334
-Mike Doyle says he'll take care of Pennsylvania voters,

00:21:18.334 --> 00:21:21.567
but can we really trust someone like Mike Doyle?

00:21:21.567 --> 00:21:24.400
-Hi, I'm Mike Doyle, and I'm a name you can trust,

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:25.701
unlike Mike Doyle.

00:21:25.701 --> 00:21:27.300
So, listen to me, Mike Doyle,

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:29.567
and stay the hell away from Mike Doyle.

00:21:29.567 --> 00:21:31.734
On Election Day, don't vote for this man,

00:21:31.734 --> 00:21:33.133
Mike Doyle -- No, wait.

00:21:33.133 --> 00:21:36.367
That's me. Avoid THIS guy. Wait. Is that me or him?

00:21:36.367 --> 00:21:38.100
[Bleep] I don't even know anymore.

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:39.200
-This has been a message from

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:40.834
the Mike Doyle Against Mike Doyle PAC.

00:21:40.834 --> 00:21:42.701
-Mike Doyle and Mike Doyle.

00:21:42.701 --> 00:21:44.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:21:48.567 --> 00:21:50.334
Well, get this, guys. I heard that Pfizer

00:21:50.334 --> 00:21:52.100
is being investigated for allegedly hiding

00:21:52.100 --> 00:21:54.100
more than a billion dollars in profit

00:21:54.100 --> 00:21:56.634
by transferring money to other countries.

00:21:56.634 --> 00:21:58.200
Yeah, not good. Well, in response,

00:21:58.200 --> 00:22:00.701
Pfizer went ahead and released this statement, and they said...

00:22:13.267 --> 00:22:14.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:22:14.267 --> 00:22:16.234
It sounds serious. -Wow.

00:22:16.234 --> 00:22:17.934
-Pfight. -Pfight.

00:22:17.934 --> 00:22:20.367
-Pfight -- Pfight me, sorry, yeah.

00:22:20.367 --> 00:22:21.834
Well, some entertainment news.

00:22:21.834 --> 00:22:24.801
Henry Cavill says that, in his next performance as Superman,

00:22:24.801 --> 00:22:28.601
he'll be playing a "enormously joyful Superman."

00:22:28.601 --> 00:22:30.968
"Enormously joyful Superman."

00:22:30.968 --> 00:22:34.434
We actually have an early clip of enormously joyful Superman.

00:22:34.434 --> 00:22:37.167
Take a look at this.

00:22:37.167 --> 00:22:40.167
-I know you're trying to find out where I hang my cape.

00:22:40.167 --> 00:22:41.567
You won't.

00:22:41.567 --> 00:22:43.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:22:46.601 --> 00:22:48.601
-Looks good. I can't wait.

00:22:48.601 --> 00:22:50.801
-I can't wait to see it. -Yeah.

00:22:50.801 --> 00:22:53.501
I saw a new report that says that people should not rake

00:22:53.501 --> 00:22:55.234
all the leaves out of their yard

00:22:55.234 --> 00:22:58.267
because it's actually better for your lawn's health.

00:22:58.267 --> 00:22:59.501
So, I think, with that in mind,

00:22:59.501 --> 00:23:01.767
it's time to say goodbye to my rake.

00:23:01.767 --> 00:23:03.601
Rake, are you there?

00:23:03.601 --> 00:23:05.801
-A lifetime of autumns together,

00:23:05.801 --> 00:23:09.501
and this is how I find out I'm fired.

00:23:09.501 --> 00:23:11.234
-Come on, rake. Don't think of it as fired.

00:23:11.234 --> 00:23:13.667
Think of it as retiring.

00:23:13.667 --> 00:23:15.834
You can now do anything you want.

00:23:15.834 --> 00:23:18.767
-Man, I want to rake leaves.

00:23:18.767 --> 00:23:21.634
Fall is my whole personality.

00:23:21.634 --> 00:23:23.634
-Look, your future is what you make it.

00:23:23.634 --> 00:23:25.033
We'll see you in the spring,

00:23:25.033 --> 00:23:26.767
when it's time to clear the flower beds.

00:23:26.767 --> 00:23:28.133
-You're right, Jimmy.

00:23:28.133 --> 00:23:30.400
Hey, we had some good times, though.

00:23:30.400 --> 00:23:31.767
Remember high school?

00:23:31.767 --> 00:23:33.267
[ Laughter ]

00:23:33.267 --> 00:23:36.968
I used to hang out with you and your friends.

00:23:36.968 --> 00:23:39.901
Watching you guys play hoops,

00:23:39.901 --> 00:23:42.100
hoping you'd take a rake break.

00:23:42.100 --> 00:23:44.968
[ Laughter ]

00:23:44.968 --> 00:23:48.634
Who was that guy that used to pour out half his Gatorade

00:23:48.634 --> 00:23:50.901
then fill the empty half with Yoohoo

00:23:50.901 --> 00:23:52.567
and call it Gator-Hoo?

00:23:52.567 --> 00:23:54.767
[ Laughter ]

00:23:54.767 --> 00:23:57.934
Ed Zipperton. Man, that guy was cool.

00:23:57.934 --> 00:23:59.567
-This has been another edition

00:23:59.567 --> 00:24:02.901
of "Making James Read Lines He's Never Seen Before."

00:24:02.901 --> 00:24:05.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:24:05.133 --> 00:24:07.467
[ Laughter ]

00:24:10.701 --> 00:24:11.968
-I miss that rake.

00:24:11.968 --> 00:24:13.200
[ Laughter ]

00:24:13.200 --> 00:24:15.000
Guys, listen to this.

00:24:15.000 --> 00:24:17.868
A new study found that, in the U.S., deli meat is linked

00:24:17.868 --> 00:24:21.334
to more than 90% of all listeria cases.

00:24:21.334 --> 00:24:23.200
Right now, the CEO of Blimpie is like,

00:24:23.200 --> 00:24:25.267
"Well, that's what you get for using real meat."

00:24:25.267 --> 00:24:26.667
[ Laughter ]

00:24:26.667 --> 00:24:28.000
Well, guys, this is very interesting.

00:24:28.000 --> 00:24:30.300
A new survey found that you can have the best chance

00:24:30.300 --> 00:24:34.234
of surviving a zombie apocalypse in Florida.

00:24:34.234 --> 00:24:35.534
I wonder why that is.

00:24:35.534 --> 00:24:37.467
-[ Scoffs ] Because even zombies

00:24:37.467 --> 00:24:39.200
are too afraid to visit Florida.

00:24:39.200 --> 00:24:40.434
[ Laughter ]

00:24:40.434 --> 00:24:43.868
-You know what? No. You know what? No.

00:24:43.868 --> 00:24:45.767
I'm tired of all the Florida slander.

00:24:45.767 --> 00:24:48.367
We always make fun of Florida, but I'm putting my foot down.

00:24:48.367 --> 00:24:51.067
It's a great state full of great people.

00:24:51.067 --> 00:24:52.734
-Listen to this next story. A Florida man

00:24:52.734 --> 00:24:57.467
is accused of spiking his co-worker's drink with bleach.

00:24:57.467 --> 00:25:00.567
-See? Florida is scary, dude.

00:25:00.567 --> 00:25:03.300
-Oh, come on. I'm sure he had a perfectly good reason.

00:25:03.300 --> 00:25:05.501
-He confessed to deputies, saying he wanted

00:25:05.501 --> 00:25:08.767
to get back at his co-worker for "being difficult."

00:25:08.767 --> 00:25:10.100
[ Laughter ]

00:25:10.100 --> 00:25:11.868
-"Being difficult"?

00:25:11.868 --> 00:25:13.133
-That's just one guy.

00:25:13.133 --> 00:25:14.400
It's a random workplace incident.

00:25:14.400 --> 00:25:15.868
Not everyone in Florida is chasing people around,

00:25:15.868 --> 00:25:17.334
trying to hurt them.

00:25:17.334 --> 00:25:20.300
-A Florida man is accused of chasing two people with knives.

00:25:20.300 --> 00:25:21.534
[ Laughter ]

00:25:21.534 --> 00:25:24.033
-You're done. You're done, man. Case closed.

00:25:24.033 --> 00:25:26.567
-I mean -- I mean, it was just only a knife.

00:25:26.567 --> 00:25:29.100
-They say he didn't stop with the knives.

00:25:29.100 --> 00:25:30.434
He also grabbed an axe.

00:25:30.434 --> 00:25:31.667
[ Laughter ]

00:25:31.667 --> 00:25:34.200
-I'm telling you, man, Florida is scary!

00:25:34.200 --> 00:25:36.601
-That's a fluke between a few people.

00:25:36.601 --> 00:25:38.634
It's not like he was knocking on doors in the wee hours

00:25:38.634 --> 00:25:40.434
of the morning while wielding a machete.

00:25:40.434 --> 00:25:43.701
-A man in a South Florida neighborhood knocking on doors

00:25:43.701 --> 00:25:47.534
in the wee hours of the morning while wielding a machete.

00:25:47.534 --> 00:25:49.300
[ Laughter ] -Come on.

00:25:49.300 --> 00:25:51.367
-Look, at least they're keeping it within state lines.

00:25:51.367 --> 00:25:53.400
You know, it's not like they're coming to your house

00:25:53.400 --> 00:25:54.934
and stealing the food out of your mouth.

00:25:54.934 --> 00:25:57.567
-Three Florida men were arrested in a multimillion-dollar

00:25:57.567 --> 00:26:01.968
theft ring of stolen meat across the Midwest.

00:26:01.968 --> 00:26:03.734
-What's your excuse this time?

00:26:03.734 --> 00:26:06.367
-Maybe they were -- they were giving the food to the needy.

00:26:06.367 --> 00:26:08.667
-The men were selling the meat on the black market.

00:26:08.667 --> 00:26:10.434
-Alright, forget it! Let's talk about something else!

00:26:10.434 --> 00:26:11.968
I'm not -- I'm tired of it!

00:26:11.968 --> 00:26:16.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:26:16.400 --> 00:26:19.501
Finally, Essentia water has teamed up

00:26:19.501 --> 00:26:20.968
with a boxed-wine company

00:26:20.968 --> 00:26:23.167
to sell water and wine in one box.

00:26:23.167 --> 00:26:24.834
Look at this.

00:26:24.834 --> 00:26:26.334
Yeah.

00:26:26.334 --> 00:26:30.033
In a related story, they're currently being sued by Jesus.

00:26:30.033 --> 00:26:31.801
This weekend is Halloween.

00:26:31.801 --> 00:26:33.067
-Ooh!

00:26:33.067 --> 00:26:35.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:26:35.467 --> 00:26:36.868
-I was so touched this morning.

00:26:36.868 --> 00:26:38.567
A kid who lives in my neighborhood

00:26:38.567 --> 00:26:41.367
put on a fake patchy beard and said he was going as me.

00:26:41.367 --> 00:26:43.467
Isn't that nice?

00:26:43.467 --> 00:26:44.901
[ Laughter ]

00:26:44.901 --> 00:26:46.701
I read that this is expected to be

00:26:46.701 --> 00:26:48.868
the biggest Halloween since the pandemic.

00:26:48.868 --> 00:26:50.167
Yeah.

00:26:50.167 --> 00:26:52.934
[ Cheers and applause ] Yeah. That's right.

00:26:52.934 --> 00:26:54.934
Now that COVID is under control,

00:26:54.934 --> 00:26:57.200
kids can safely return to eating food from strangers.

00:26:57.200 --> 00:26:59.634
That's what I'm talking about.

00:26:59.634 --> 00:27:01.701
People are going all-out.

00:27:01.701 --> 00:27:03.267
I saw that costume spending alone

00:27:03.267 --> 00:27:06.567
projected to hit a record of $3.6 billion.

00:27:06.567 --> 00:27:08.367
[ Audience oohs ] 3.6 billion.

00:27:08.367 --> 00:27:10.133
To put that in perspective,

00:27:10.133 --> 00:27:12.734
that's almost half as much as Kanye lost this week.

00:27:12.734 --> 00:27:14.834
-Oh. -$3.6 billion.

00:27:14.834 --> 00:27:17.300
A lot of --

00:27:17.300 --> 00:27:20.367
Almost half. [ Laughs ]

00:27:20.367 --> 00:27:22.200
That's right. Halloween is almost here.

00:27:22.200 --> 00:27:23.734
You probably heard a lot of good advice

00:27:23.734 --> 00:27:25.133
about how to safely enjoy the holiday,

00:27:25.133 --> 00:27:26.367
but you have to be on the alert

00:27:26.367 --> 00:27:28.400
because there's a lot of bad advice out there, too.

00:27:28.400 --> 00:27:30.167
So, here with some terrible Halloween advice

00:27:30.167 --> 00:27:32.067
is our sound engineer, Steve Mandel.

00:27:32.067 --> 00:27:33.567
Steve?

00:27:33.567 --> 00:27:36.901
-Only trick-or-treat at houses with large dogs.

00:27:36.901 --> 00:27:38.300
If they bite,

00:27:38.300 --> 00:27:41.367
you could be looking at a pretty sweet lawsuit.

00:27:41.367 --> 00:27:42.601
[ Laughter ]

00:27:42.601 --> 00:27:44.367
-Thank you very much.

00:27:44.367 --> 00:27:46.000
Thank you very much, Steve.

00:27:46.000 --> 00:27:48.033
[ Applause ]

00:27:48.033 --> 00:27:49.868
[ Laughter ] Let's get to some news.

00:27:49.868 --> 00:27:51.467
Everybody's talking about this.

00:27:51.467 --> 00:27:55.334
Last night, Elon Musk finally closed his deal to buy Twitter.

00:27:55.334 --> 00:27:56.834
[ Audience groans ] Yeah.

00:27:56.834 --> 00:27:59.701
Now he owns SpaceX if he wants to see the heavens,

00:27:59.701 --> 00:28:01.767
